2026-09-27T11:25:26.9244072Z Update Note
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9244267Z ===========
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9244568Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9244830Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9244930Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9245135Z ================
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9245260Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9245405Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9245755Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9245968Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9246079Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9246342Z ====================================
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9246502Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9246639Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9247021Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9247772Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9248476Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9248992Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9249094Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9249516Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9250045Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9250309Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9250600Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9250986Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9251077Z Packages
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9251263Z ========
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9251376Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9252612Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9253913Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9254126Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9254584Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9255395Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9326751Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9328036Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9329000Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9330230Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9330419Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9330720Z ==========================
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9330879Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9331920Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9333106Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9333754Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9334608Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T11:25:26.9334829Z 
